# File: tests/blender/test_contract_*.py and tests/unit/quality/test_contract_gate.py (scenarios map 1:1 to tests)
# Generated from: specs/30-add-contract-validation-re-import-check-and-review-renders/requirements.md
Feature: Contract validation, re-import check, and review renders

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Validation reports every checkable contract rule
    Given a compliant "Crate" asset collection of class "standard_prop"
    When contract validation runs
    Then the report passes with snapshots for every object and no findings

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: Each failure class is detected
    Given a "Crate" fixture with <defect>
    When contract validation runs
    Then the report fails with rule "<rule>" naming the affected object or material and a remediation

    Examples:
      | defect                                   | rule                   |
      | an unapplied root rotation               | transform.root_applied |
      | an origin away from bottom center        | pivot.bottom_center    |
      | no UV map                                | uv.single_map          |
      | overlapping UVs                          | uv.overlap             |
      | a Noise Texture material                 | material.node_types    |
      | Position-driven texture coordinates      | material.uv_coordinates |
      | a 4000-triangle Mobile LOD0              | budget.tris            |
      | a Mobile name that differs from Desktop  | variants.names_match   |

  @SCN003
  Scenario: The re-import check compares exported FBX against the pre-export report
    Given an exported Crate variant folder and its pre-export report
    When the re-import check runs in a fresh headless Blender
    Then it passes
    When T_Crate_Body_BC.png is deleted and the check runs again
    Then it fails with rule "reimport.texture_missing" naming the file

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Review renders are written to a known folder
    Given "Crate" and "Crate_Mobile" collections
    When review renders run into an output folder
    Then front, back, side, and three_quarter PNGs exist for desktop and mobile
    And the user's scenes are unchanged

  @SCN005
  Scenario: The texture proof sheet compares baked, re-imported, and pre-bake looks
    Given an exported Crate variant folder and a pre-bake render
    When the texture proof runs
    Then Crate_proof.png shows the pre-bake, baked, and re-imported renders side by side

  @SCN006
  Scenario: The gate helper stops finalize on failure
    Given a failing contract report and a failing re-import report
    When gate runs on each
    Then it raises "quality.contract_failed" and "quality.reimport_mismatch" with the findings and report

  @SCN007
  Scenario: One implementation is reachable from operators and the CLI
    Given the add-on is enabled
    When validate_contract runs as an operator and as a direct contract_core call on the same asset
    Then both reports are identical
    And the contract CLI exits 2 with a remediation when Blender can't be found
